frica with low prices and vast product ranges. Businesses and unions warn the growth could come at a cost for local jobs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa airline behind viral stadium flyby scraps repeat display</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9aa720147e9a769596996970f75d9f49d5d4d48e82a170cfa62086b8ec544d26</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-airline-behind-viral-stadium-flyby-scraps-repeat-display/a-78870028--69daa320153e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-airline-behind-viral-stadium-flyby-scraps-repeat-display/a-78870028?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two passenger jets passed close to Cape Town's DHL Stadium during a flyover last weekend. The carrier said it has shelved plans to repeat the display as South Africa's aviation authority investigates the event.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: Tens of thousands rally over Ceuta crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4909723263e944855efd52b4a0fc8479a6cacfbcdfd2d4c8c0ad91c381a46a25</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T23:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-tens-of-thousands-rally-over-ceuta-crisis/a-78814756--b0db1adff664.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-tens-of-thousands-rally-over-ceuta-crisis/a-78814756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tensions continue over migrants still stranded in Ceuta and the Sanchez government’s handling of the fallout.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tunisia's activists decry civil society crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45b2aa639ae75339b259812c6a3d61b0271114ccefb8a98c03c0366d76e07db4</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T04:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tunisia-s-activists-decry-civil-society-crackdown/a-78614966--e657463dce69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tunisia-s-activists-decry-civil-society-crackdown/a-78614966?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Five years into Tunisian President Kais Saied’s increasingly authoritarian rule, rights groups warn that the country’s once vibrant civil society is being silenced.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Congo's Ebola caseload tops 6,000 as concerns grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b159f65ace57a8ff417fe8c57819bf0501cd173a945fc4562a47e786ceeb4de0</id><updated>2026-09-04T19:01:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447--5f990f71c7d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo has surpassed 6,000 confirmed cases, with nearly 3,000 deaths. As the virus spreads, authorities are racing to contain one of the deadliest outbreaks in history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
